---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageMeta from '@/components/PageMeta.astro';
import GatewayCard from '@/components/ia/GatewayCard.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Working-group member guide"
  description="How SPDTF working-group members get access, use Teams, submit evidence, join meetings and review model candidates."
>
  <PageMeta category="Working groups · Member guide" variant="brand" updated="Current guidance · 21 August 2026" />
  <h1>Working-group member guide</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    This guide explains the common participation pattern for SPDTF working groups.
    It covers access, discussions, source material, meetings and model review without
    exposing private workspace links or treating participation as standards authority.
  </p>

  <div class="card-grid">
    <GatewayCard
      href="/spdtf/working-groups/member-guide/getting-started"
      eyebrow="Access"
      title="Getting started"
      description="Understand registration, membership, invitations, accounts, roles and support."
    />
    <GatewayCard
      href="/spdtf/working-groups/member-guide/teams-and-discussions"
      eyebrow="Discuss"
      title="Teams and discussions"
      description="Choose the right channel, keep one issue in one thread and use page comments appropriately."
    />
    <GatewayCard
      href="/spdtf/working-groups/member-guide/source-material-and-sharepoint"
      eyebrow="Contribute"
      title="Source material and SharePoint"
      description="Use the private organisation intake area and supply evidence with provenance and restrictions."
    />
    <GatewayCard
      href="/spdtf/working-groups/member-guide/meetings-and-records"
      eyebrow="Participate"
      title="Meetings and records"
      description="Prepare, contribute, support asynchronous follow-up and handle transcripts safely."
    />
    <GatewayCard
      href="/spdtf/working-groups/member-guide/model-review-and-decisions"
      eyebrow="Review"
      title="Model review and decisions"
      description="Challenge candidates in business language and understand who may decide what."
    />
  </div>

  <h2 id="current-status">What is current, and what is proposed</h2>
  <p>
    The guide combines several decisions, but it does not give every source the same
    maturity. Use the status in this table when a detailed page refers to a process.
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Area</th><th>Status</th><th>What members can rely on</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Working-group topology</td><td>Accepted · ADR-0063</td><td>Eight modelling groups with bounded responsibilities.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Public recruitment</td><td>Accepted · ADR-0069</td><td>An expression of interest is reviewed before access is granted.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Teams and SharePoint pattern</td><td>Accepted · ADR-0070</td><td>A private Team for discussion and a separate, organisation-isolated evidence intake.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Email support and intake fallback</td><td>Accepted · ADR-0072</td><td>Bounded access support and screened attachments for authorised participants.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Evidence-to-model method</td><td>Proposed · ADR-0065</td><td>Useful working method, but not a ratified lifecycle. ADR-0065 remains proposed.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Consensus and ratification</td><td>Proposed · ADR-0068</td><td>Do not treat its stages or time windows as operative. ADR-0068 remains proposed.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2 id="workspace-status">Workspace status is not group authority</h2>
  <p>
    The Finance and Banking modelling workspace is implemented. The separate,
    cross-cutting Technology Working Group workspace is also implemented. The other
    seven modelling workspaces are planned. Technology Working Group is not a ninth
    modelling context and is not the Property Technology working group.
  </p>
  <p>
    Implemented workspace infrastructure does not mean a group is convened, has agreed
    a model, or can ratify a standard. Each workspace page states its own roster,
    candidate and decision status; where these are not recorded, they remain unconfirmed.
  </p>

  <h2 id="routes">Where to go next</h2>
  <p>
    Browse the <a href="/spdtf/working-groups">eight group workspaces</a> for scope,
    evidence, questions and review records. If you are not yet a member, the public
    <a href="/working-groups/join">working-group sign-up form</a> records an expression
    of interest; it does not confer membership, Microsoft access or decision rights.
  </p>
</Layout>
